<Project>

  <!--
    Copies the vendored parakeet.cpp binaries from the repository's native/ directory into the
    build output, preserving the native/<rid>/<backend>/ shape the loader searches for.

    Without this, `dotnet run` cannot find a library placed at the repository root: the loader
    searches relative to AppContext.BaseDirectory, which for a normal build is
    bin/<config>/<tfm>/, not the repository root.

    Note the glob is evaluated when the project is evaluated, so a binary dropped into native/
    after a build needs another build before it appears in the output.

    LICENSE is copied for a different reason than the binaries, and it is not optional. Every
    parakeet.cpp `lib-` archive ships one, and the library is MIT: "The above copyright notice and
    this permission notice shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the
    Software." Copying parakeet.dll and leaving its LICENSE behind redistributes an MIT binary
    without the notice MIT requires, which is a licence breach rather than an untidy output
    directory. It travels beside the binary it covers — one per backend directory, so a drop that
    vendors only some backends still ships exactly the notices it needs.

    This only holds if the LICENSE is on disk in the first place. Unpacking just parakeet.dll out
    of the archive puts the breach back and nothing here can detect it; NATIVE-BINARIES.md in the project notes
    says so where the unpacking is described.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../native/**/*.dll;
                   $(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../native/**/*.so;
                   $(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../native/**/*.dylib;
                   $(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../native/**/LICENSE"
          Link="native/%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)"
          CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest"
          Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
